# Qwen3.5-9B — campaign model 04. THE MEMORY-CONSTRAINED ONE.   [E2E-5]
# Sourced by run_model_campaign.sh; see models.d/README.md for the rules.
MODEL_KEY=qwen35_9b
MODEL_PATH=/mnt/nvmes/nvme1/models/Qwen3.5-9B
SERVED_NAME=Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B
VLLM_ENV=modern                 # Qwen3_5ForConditionalGeneration is NOT in 0.9.1
# measured: longest sh_64k prompt = 49,195 tokens (3.45 chars/token) - above
# 48k, so 48000 was never viable for this model either. At 56k the KV cost is
# still small: only 8 of 32 layers are full-attention, 4 KV heads x 256 dim,
# fp8 => ~0.9 GiB. The 24 linear-attention layers hold a fixed-size recurrent
# state, not a per-token cache, which is why a 9B fits a 24 GiB card at all.
MAX_MODEL_LEN=57344
# 19.3 GB of bf16 weights on a 23.99 GiB card. The KV cache is small for its
# size - only 8 of 32 layers are full-attention (full_attention_interval 4),
# 4 KV heads x 256 head_dim, fp8 => well under 1 GiB at this context - so the
# binding constraint is weights + activations, not cache. 0.95 is deliberate,
# and it is safe only because nothing else runs on GPU1: this campaign reads
# fact vectors from the committed embedding cache, so no embedding server.
GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.95
# MEASURED with diagnose_serving.sh, three cells, ten unique-stratum questions:
#     fp8  + enable_thinking=false   10/10   'pesäpallo'
#     auto + enable_thinking=false   10/10   'pesäpallo'
#     fp8  + thinking LEFT ON         0/10   'Thinking Process:\n\n1.  **Analyze'
# Both dtypes are healthy AND both fit at 56k on a 24 GiB card, so the choice
# is free and goes to BF16: there are reports of Qwen3.5 degradation under some
# cache configurations, nothing here needs the memory fp8 would save, and BF16
# matches the two Gemma models.
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=auto
# THE LOAD-BEARING FLAG. The harness allows the model GENERATION_MAX_TOKENS=10
# output tokens - the benchmark's own generation_max_length. A thinking model
# spends all ten on reasoning and scores ~0, which would look like a model
# result and would actually be a serving-mode artifact. This model's chat
# template honours enable_thinking=false, so it is served in its non-thinking
# instruct mode - the only mode in which the frozen harness can measure it.
# preflight_model.py fails the model if any reasoning marker still appears.
EXTRA_SERVE_FLAGS='--language-model-only --skip-mm-profiling --attention-backend TRITON_ATTN --default-chat-template-kwargs {"enable_thinking":false}'
NOTES="9B hybrid Gated-DeltaNet/full attention (3 linear : 1 full, 8 full of 32 layers), 262k native context served at 56k; thinking disabled at the server; BF16 only - if it does not fit, record the hardware constraint, do NOT substitute a quantized checkpoint."

# Two further notes specific to this architecture:
#
# * PREFIX CACHING for the Mamba/GDN-style recurrent cache is documented as
#   experimental. The frozen substrate already serves --no-enable-prefix-caching
#   for determinism, so the campaign does not touch that path at all. Do not
#   turn it on here for throughput.
# * The REASONING PARSER is deliberately not enabled, and the measurement above
#   shows why that is safe AND why it was not the check that proved it. With
#   thinking left on this model emits PROSE reasoning - "Thinking Process:" -
#   with no tag and an empty `reasoning_content`, so `no_reasoning` passed it
#   and the ten-question accuracy FLOOR is what caught it, at 0/10. A reasoning
#   parser would not have helped either: there is no tag for it to split on.
#   Disabling thinking at the chat-template level is the fix, and the floor is
#   the guard that verifies it stayed disabled.
# * Vendor sampling guidance (temperature/top_p/top_k) is NOT adopted. The
#   campaign's temperature 0 / max_tokens 10 is a deliberate frozen
#   experimental control shared by every model, not an oversight.
